Model a deployment system.

A Server has a name and a status — either "online" or "offline". Servers start online.

deploy(app_name) — deploys an app to the server. It must fail if the server is offline, and must fail if that app is already deployed there.
remove(app_name) — removes a deployed app; fails if it isn't deployed.
take_offline() / bring_online() — change status.
A read-only app_count showing how many apps are deployed.
Printing a server should show something readable.

Then a ServerFleet that holds many servers:

add_server(server)
deploy_to_all(app_name) — deploys to every online server, skipping offline ones, and reports how many succeeded.
find_server(name) — returns the server or None.
offline_servers() — the names of all offline servers.
total_apps() — total apps deployed across the fleet.